/E (consulted were very reluctant to risk performing a procedure to remove it. Medication and radiation therapy helped to subdue it, but eventually this cyst began to affect a nerve in my leg. I was in pain, I struggled to function, and soon I could only hobble around on crutches. The bottom line was that for nearly all of 1974, I was out of commission. Instead of studying Torah in yeshivah, I was in the hospital or in bed at my home in Los Angeles. I had been hoping to join some friends who had gone to study at the Lubavitch yeshivah on Ocean Parkway in Flatbush, New York, but it just wasn't possible.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [27]
