>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The Torah doesn't just present the problem. It has solutions. Genesis offers three different responses to the misuse of intelligence and power.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The first is the Flood. When a creation becomes destructive beyond repair, sometimes you have to shut it down and start again. Not everything we are capable of creating should be allowed to continue.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The second is the Tower of Babel. When humanity united its powers for the wrong purpose, G-d divided them, confused their languages and scattered them across the earth. Sometimes the answer is not destruction but decentralisation. Don't allow too much power to be concentrated in one place.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The third is Abraham. This is the ideal. Rather than continually intervening to stop humanity from going wrong, G-d introduces us to a man who chooses to live according to a higher moral code, and who teaches that code to others. The ultimate solution is not to control intelligence from the outside, but to instil a moral compass that guides it from within.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (These are three very relevant principles for the AI age. Know when to pull the plug. Don't concentrate unlimited power in one place. And above all, make sure our technological advances are guided by moral values.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (The answers to our biggest questions, even in this robotic age, can still be found in a handwritten scroll given to us over three thousand years ago. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (AI can do our laundry, and may even perform open-heart surgery one day. But it can't do morality for us. That is one responsibility we must never outsource.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
